00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.540
Leah: Let’s now look at Kanban starting with its strengths

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:12.280
Chris: Easy to learn and use -Kanban is very straightforward
with its approach and is easy to learn and use.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:18.320
It can be used in small simple projects such as for
children to help plan their homework; to complex

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.150
business projects using the Scrum framework.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:28.370
Leah: Visual-It is a visual system, and the flow
of work is managed using a Kanban project board.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.250
In its simplest form there are three columns which
are labelled: ‘To Do’, ‘In Progress’, and ‘Done’.

00:00:35.139 --> 00:00:41.460
Chris: Adaptable and flexible-It is adaptable and
flexible as there can be no planned timings and

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.240
priorities and workload can be changed during the project.

00:00:45.849 --> 00:00:50.280
It is also flexible in that it can be
used with another framework such as Scrum.

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:57.070
Leah: Collaborative-As a simple visual system,
it helps the project team to collaborate as it

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:03.010
simplifies planning, helps to manage work and
inventory, and increase productivity and efficiency.

00:01:03.469 --> 00:01:09.130
Chris: Low overheads-It has low overheads as
there is no training needed and all you need

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.639
is a Kanban project board to get started.

00:01:12.699 --> 00:01:17.860
Leah: Reduces costs and waste-As it can be
used with LEAN’s ‘Just In Time’ methodology

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.780
it helps to reduce cost and waste.

00:01:21.849 --> 00:01:22.830
Chris: And the Weaknesses

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:31.870
Needs another framework to work-Kanban would need a
framework such as Scrum or LEAN ‘Just in Time’ to work

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.690
as it needs the supporting elements that they would give.

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:41.270
Leah: Not suitable on plans that are not
stable-Kanban would need plans that are stable

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:47.220
and consistent to work effectively, so this may
be an issue if the plans need to be dynamic.

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:54.390
Chris: Is not Iterative-Another framework would
be needed for iterations to be used which would

00:01:54.390 --> 00:02:00.510
normally end up being a separate project, as iteration
is not essential to Kanban at a ticket level.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:06.729
Leah: Lack of timing-Because Kanban is
adaptable and flexible, there are often no

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.089
planned timings for each stage of the project.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:14.860
This also means that items can be changed
during the project, and this could cause issues.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:21.600
Chris: A Kanban project could be as simple as cleaning
your house or planning school homework or college exams.

00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:29.399
In the workplace examples could include giving a project
manager visibility to a project status; using a Kanban

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:36.370
board to delegate work across a team; or connecting related
work items across different projects or project boards.

